2025-09-30","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NJ"},{"bioguideId":"P000614","fullName":"Rep. Pappas, Chris [D-NH-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-12-19","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NH"},{"bioguideId":"S000168","fullName":"Rep. Salazar, Maria Elvira [R-FL-27]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-01-13","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"FL"},{"bioguideId":"G000583","fullName":"Rep. Gottheimer, Josh [D-NJ-5]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-03-24","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NJ"},{"bioguideId":"S001226","fullName":"Rep. Salinas, Andrea [D-OR-6]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-04-14","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"OR"},{"bioguideId":"S001218","fullName":"Rep. Stansbury, Melanie A. [D-NM-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-04-27","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NM"},{"bioguideId":"J000295","fullName":"Rep. Joyce, David P. [R-OH-14]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-08-03","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"OH"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T20:26:53+00:00","id":"hr2149-119","introducedDate":"2025-03-14","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-03-14","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Veterans' Affairs."},"laws":[],"number":"2149","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Armed Forces and National Security","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"M001219","district":null,"fullName":"Del. Moylan, James C. [R-GU-At Large]","party":"R","state":"GU"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-03-14","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><b>Correcting Guam's History in the PACT Act</b></p> <p>This bill expands eligibility for a presumption of service-connection for specified diseases associated with exposure to certain herbicide agents. Under a presumption of service-connection, specific conditions diagnosed in certain veterans are presumed to have been caused by the circumstances of their military service. Health care benefits and disability compensation may then be awarded.</p> <p>Under the bill, service performed in Guam or its territorial waters between August 15, 1958, and July 31, 1980, provides a veteran who has a specified disease that is associated with exposure to certain herbicide agents with eligibility for a presumption of service-connection. (Under current law, the eligible time frame for service in Guam is between January 9, 1962, and July 31, 1980.)</p>","updateDate":"2025-06-17T19:42:44Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Correcting Guam’s History in the PACT Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-08-04T08:07:08Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-08-04T08:07:08Z"}
